/-!
# Draisma--Vargas Part I: gonality of graphs up to subdivision

Every connected finite graph of genus `g` has a regular subdivision carrying a divisor of degree
`⌈g/2⌉ + 1` and rank at least one
(`DraismaVargas.graph_regularSubdivisionGonality_le_ceil_half_genus_add_one`). More generally, a
connected core with positive integer edge lengths, a rational metric graph up to scale, has a
common refinement carrying such a divisor
(`DraismaVargas.regularSubdivisionGonality_le_ceil_half_genus_add_one`); in even genus at least
six the construction gives an explicit scale
(`DraismaVargas.nonempty_evenSubdivisionPencil_ceil_half_genus_add_one`).

This is the finite-graph, divisorial form of the main theorem of J. Draisma and A. Vargas,
*Catalan-many tropical morphisms to trees; Part I: Constructions*, arXiv:1909.12924, which bounds
the gonality of metric graphs by `⌈g/2⌉ + 1`. The invariant used here,
`Utilities.Gonality.regularSubdivisionGonality`, is the least degree of a rank-one divisor on some
regular subdivision. Identifying it with the metric divisorial gonality is a separate theorem and
is not formalized.

## Structure

* `Statement`: the headline theorems.
* `LowGenus`: genus at most five, from the Atanasov--Ranganathan theorem (library `LowGenus`).
* `OddGenusTwoCycle`, `OddGenusRetraction`: odd genus reduces to even genus by attaching a digon
  at a vertex and retracting the divisor to the original graph.
* `Infrastructure/`: gluing data for tropical morphisms to trees — sheet partitions, gluing,
  contraction and its ramification, and realization at rational edge lengths.
* `LocalCases/`: the even-genus construction. It starts from a caterpillar-of-loops seed, walks
  through the walls of the space of metric graphs by Whitehead moves, resolves the local
  configuration at every wall type, and transports the resulting pencil back to the requested
  core. The walk follows A. Vargas, *Catalan-many tropical morphisms to trees; Part II: A space and
  a count*, arXiv:2609.09109.

Add an import line above whenever a module is added under `DraismaVargas/`, or
`lake build DraismaVargas` will silently skip it.
-/
